diff --git a/docs/api.md b/docs/api.md
index 149f5dd..545a00a 100644
--- a/docs/api.md
+++ b/docs/api.md
@@ -153,3 +153,41 @@ For operators. Every notification the service has enqueued, by state:
 ### Health: `GET /health`
 
 `{ "status": "ok" }` while the service answers.
+
+## Assign a ticket
+
+`PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` accepts `{"assignee":"Sam"}` or `{"assignee":null}`.
+Names are trimmed, single-line, non-empty text of at most 64 characters. Only open and
+in-progress tickets allow assignment changes (otherwise 409). The response is the
+updated ticket. Every ticket includes `assignee`, initially null. Repeating the same
+assignment has no side effects. Each actual assignment notifies the new agent via
+the outbox and records the change in the audit log. Unassigning sends no notification.
+
+`GET /tickets?assignee=Sam` filters by agent; `?assignee=` selects unassigned tickets.
+This combines with status and priority filters and cursor pagination.
+
+## Import tickets
+
+`POST /tickets/import` accepts `{"tickets":[{"title":"Printer","requester":"Sam"}]}`.
+Each item has the same fields and validation as `POST /tickets`; priority is optional.
+The array may be empty and may contain at most 5000 items. The first invalid item
+produces a 400 error naming its zero-based index, with no tickets, audit entries,
+notifications or IDs consumed. Success returns 201 with `{"created":1,"ids":["T-0001"]}`.
+Tickets are created in input order, audited with the request actor, and notify their
+requesters through the normal outbox. The entire batch is saved once.
+
+The import endpoint accepts bodies up to 16 MiB (or MAX_BODY_BYTES if larger),
+so a full batch works with default configuration. Other endpoints keep MAX_BODY_BYTES.
+
+## Due times and overdue tickets
+
+When `DUE_TIMES=on`, every ticket response includes `due` as a UTC ISO timestamp.
+It is computed once from creation plus the configured priority response hours:
+urgent 4, high 24, normal 72, low 168 by default. Later priority changes, reopenings,
+and response-hour configuration changes preserve the stored due time. Imports use
+the same calculation.
+
+`GET /tickets?overdue=true` keeps open and in-progress tickets with `due` strictly
+before the current server time. It combines with every other filter and pagination.
+`overdue=false` applies no overdue restriction; other values are 400 errors.
+With the switch off, `due` is omitted and `overdue` remains an ignored parameter.
